waydroid-host-stack: an LE link can have several owners.

A guest connect whose requester had gone could finish after another guest
client reused the link (BlueZ reports it connected, then ServicesResolved
comes later); its ownership then replaced the reuser's, and cleaning up its
dead socket dropped the link 2 s into the reuser's GATT discovery.  Seen on
the Pro1x with a Tesla's phone key, 2026-11-20: "LE device already connected
- reuse", then "guest client gone: dropped its LE link".  The link is now
dropped only when its last owner goes.  Tests: cargo test (service::), new
shared_link_dropped_only_by_its_last_owner.  Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix,
2026-11-23), on d9a316e (MIT).

